cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use SIRIUS in your research or work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "SIRIUS: Measurement-driven fine-tuning of a 0.5B local security auditor"
abstract: >-
  SIRIUS is a local-first security-auditing assistant built on
  Qwen2.5-0.5B-Instruct. The repository contains the complete measurement,
  diagnosis, consultation, fine-tuning and acceptance pipeline: GGUF
  telemetry, a 34-item security baseline, a dual retention/task gate,
  LABEL-first contrastive training data, and the final Q6_K/Q5_K_M GGUF
  artifacts description. The resulting model improves the baseline score
  from 0.753 to 0.795 and fixes 4 of 5 systematic vulnerability-label errors.
authors:
  - family-names: Ahmed
    given-names: Tayyab
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-20
